A||||12||Smokin87||Which cars had the DUKE||||5||
Z||000000||Smokin87||01-21-2001||01:17 AM||||I know this is a stupid question, but im a retart, and have to ask, which fieros have the duke?  and what is the difference between the duke, and another engine?||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||01-21-2001||01:51 AM||||The name Duke or Iron Duke is just a nickname for the 2.5L 4 cylinder engine offered in the Fiero and many other '80's GM vehicles.<P>All '84 Fieros have the Duke......all base models came with the Duke as standard equipment with the V-6 being optional on most models.  <P>All GT's had the V-6 as standard equipment.  <P>'85-'87 SE's could be had with the Duke or V-6 (Duke was standard).<P>The '87 & '88 Dukes have distributorless ignitions (DIS) and are generally more reliable than the '84-'86 Dukes.<BR> <BR>I know this is more info than you wanted, but what the heck!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||01-21-2001||07:08 AM||||In the mid '80s, GM renamed the Iron Duke, "Tech 4".  Same motor (basically), different handle.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||01-21-2001||10:50 AM||||I believe the renamimg of the motor happened in 87 with the intro of the DIS ignition.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Motorhead||01-22-2001||05:52 PM||||Didn't '87 also introduce the counter-balance on the engine?  Harmonics get pretty strange on the early motor at around 2500 RPM.<P>------------------<BR>"The one who dies with the most toys wins!"<BR>  bluewater46@hotmail.com<BR>1986 coupe<BR>1984 coupe<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1372350&a=10234998&p=38686771&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||danny boy||01-22-2001||07:01 PM|||| My '86 coupe had a Tech4 sticker on the air cleaner when I got it, and it had a distributer so it must have been called that before '87. Come to think of it my '87 coupe didn't have a sticker...Dealer put it on there?||||reg||1
